Lab Material
Lab 3: IdM Client Enrollment and Configuration
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the fundamentals of Identity Management (IdM) client enrollment
Successfully enroll a RHEL system as an IdM client using ipa-client-install
Configure System Security Services Daemon (SSSD) for centralized authentication
Implement Kerberos authentication for secure user access
Verify authentication functionality using kinit command
Troubleshoot common IdM client configuration issues
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with RHEL/CentOS system administration
Knowledge of network configuration concepts
Understanding of DNS resolution and hostname configuration
Basic knowledge of authentication concepts (users, groups, passwords)
Access to a functioning IdM server (covered in previous labs)
